invariant: INV-26
file: aes_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aes-equiv
reason: the x86-64 AES-128 key expansion starts from the second round
  constant, so every round key after the key itself takes the constant of
  the round after its own, and every Initial packet and AES-128-GCM record
  runs under a schedule FIPS 197 does not define. bin/aes_equiv_test
  compares each schedule with the table's byte for byte. Both
  architectures read the line, and the script builds that binary for each
  and runs it under qemu.

--- old
    store_block(round_keys, round_key);
    uint8_t round_constant = 0x01;
--- new
    store_block(round_keys, round_key);
    uint8_t round_constant = 0x02;
